    "q-74216": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74216",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274391/assets/15da2a7bcb642ecc6f5e8d584e89bee3d1002e6f5e31c85b27db0b337553ebbb.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is also a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
