      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"step-q74216\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 9</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-74216\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Which of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"51\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3F\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>?</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </p>\n</div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74216-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74216-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74216-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74216-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">III only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74216-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II and III only</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/incorrect-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectText\">Incorrect</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>Let's analyze each diagram in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Diagram I represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"52\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Diagram II represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is also a subspace of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"53\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Diagram III represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram III is not a subspace of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"54\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
